          "kicker": "Honours revoked",
          "heading": "Former Scotland captain Stuart Hogg has MBE stripped over domestic abuse conviction",
          "body": "Stuart Hogg, who won 100 Scotland caps and toured three times with the British & Irish Lions, had his MBE cancelled in March after pleading guilty to a domestic abuse charge involving his estranged wife. The honour, awarded in the 2024 New Year Honours for services to rugby, was removed from the official register. He is one of 15 people to lose honours in 2026, and was handed a one-year community payback order in January 2025."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France's Thomas Ramos out of autumn Nations Championship with thigh injury",
