          "heading": "Wallabies slip to seventh in world rankings, behind Scotland, after Bledisloe losses",
          "body": "Australia are now seventh in the World Rugby rankings, having dropped below Scotland after back-to-back Bledisloe Cup defeats to New Zealand. Those are the first two losses of the Les Kiss era, which ended an unbeaten run featuring wins over Japan, Argentina and South Africa, and the scorelines were 50-19 at Eden Park and 43-21 in Sydney. The slide lands ahead of the England Test at Twickenham and next year's home World Cup."
